From 516efb4ea8c5e413c6acf538347babc19a93cc90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:51:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: draw PQ bitmap subtitles into the Dolby Vision
 picture

Bitmap subtitles of a PQ stream (PGS in a UHD remux; the subtitle stream
inherits the video's SMPTE 2084 transfer, so m_isHDROverlay is set) are
drawn by RenderHDROverlays() onto the window framebuffer right after the
video, outside the GUI pass. With native Dolby Vision output the video
is in the PQ texture of the bridge, and PresentRender() packs that
texture into the window framebuffer with blending off, overwriting
everything drawn there: PGS subtitles never reached the TV, while text
subtitles, which go through the GUI pass and CompositeGui(), did. Seen
on hardware with Toy Story 5 (profile 7 FEL): a Latin American Spanish
PGS track showed nothing, the text tracks worked.

While DV output is captured and the frame is in the PQ texture, bind
the PQ framebuffer around RenderHDROverlays(), with the clip-space Y of
the projection flipped as CompositeGui() does for the GUI, and restore
framebuffer, viewport, scissor test and projection afterwards. The
overlays land after the video and before the GUI composite, as on the
ordinary HDR path. Their palette stays PQ, which matches the picture.
The limited-range encode of HDR overlays is skipped during DV output,
like the DV GUI composite already does.
